										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<img width="1280" height="720" src="https://i0.wp.com/uncommoncore.co/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/youtube.png?fit=1280%2C720&amp;ssl=1" class="webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image" alt="" style="display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear:both;max-width: 100%;" link_thumbnail="" decoding="async" srcset="https://i0.wp.com/uncommoncore.co/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/youtube.png?w=1280&amp;ssl=1 1280w, https://i0.wp.com/uncommoncore.co/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/youtube.png?resize=768%2C432&amp;ssl=1 768w" sizes="(max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px" />
<figure class="wp-block-audio"><audio controls src="https://uncommoncore.co/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/UCC_JordiAlexander_Mix02-1.mp3"></audio></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Today, we welcome <a href="https://twitter.com/gametheorizing">Jordi Alexander</a>, a former professional poker player turned macro trader turned crypto trader. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Jordi competes in the Mind Sports Olympiad and is an expert in games and game theory in general. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Together we discuss</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list"><li>How to pick up new games and improve</li><li>How you can apply game theory to the crypto markets</li><li>What Jordi and Su think about the market, especially the role of Bitcoin &amp; Ethereum</li><li>Why Su is Doge-pilled and whether he can convince us of his thesis</li></ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Enjoy!</p>



